  "result": "Shell completion now handles `#` in arguments. The fix is one line in `src/click/shell_completion.py`.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` uses `shlex` in whitespace-split mode, and `shlex` treats `#` as a comment start by default. So `cmd foo#bar baz` was split as `['cmd', 'foo']`, and everything after the `#` was dropped.\n\n**Fix:** I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` so `#` is an ordinary character. Quoted `#` already worked, and it still does.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `cmd foo#bar baz` now gives `['cmd', 'foo#bar', 'baz']`. Before the fix it gave `['cmd', 'foo']`.\n- I added three cases to `test_split_arg_string` in `tests/test_parser.py`: an unquoted `#` mid-word, a quoted `#`, and a standalone `#b` token.\n- Full suite: 1909 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed, 0 failed.\n\nI did not add a `CHANGES.md` entry or commit anything. Let me know if you want either.",
